From 4c025c51555eb2593155f6811c3932110594e803 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "sh.chao" <sh.chao@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 15:12:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] r25-2-0094: preserve visibility-scoped line commands

Extend r25-2-0093 after Q16 proved that rejecting all marked content produces zero native coverage. Record pointer-free visibility-run ordinals for exact later OCG checks, preserve source endpoints and translation components without changing matrix arithmetic, and retain arbitrary affine matrices through the existing bitwise intern table.

Classify every fail-closed rejection in the existing parser append, cap retained program data at 96 MiB plus independent table limits, and keep the representation shadow-only so canonical PDFium remains the sole pixel owner. Add tests for marked-content runs, exact translation storage, matrix/state interning, and canonical transparency/fill fallback.
